From April 2025 to February 2026, I interned as a Full-stack Software Developer at Amber Creative, a digital marketing agency in Singapore. During my internship, I worked on platforms that real people use every day.

## Many Platforms, Many Tech Stacks

Within ten months, I contributed to ITE's Work-Study Diploma platform, the KiasuParents community website, Glovida-RX's prescription management platform, as well as the websites for IAL and IAL InLab.

Almost every project used a different combination of tools. Most of them were built with Next.js and TypeScript, but I also worked with C# and Kentico CMS, WordPress, Strapi CMS, StoryBlok and GraphQL.

## Working in Someone Else's Codebase

Client platforms already exist before you join the project. Most of my work was building new pages and features within them, fixing bugs and making sure that a change in one place did not break something somewhere else. This taught me to read code carefully before writing any of my own.

## Why It Matters

My internship is where I learnt how to ship features to real users. It led me straight into freelance work, and eventually to building my own app, StillGood.
